The question involves comparing two types of beasts, Dhampir and Gorgon, based on their base attributes. We need to find the mean values of these attributes for each type and then compare them. The base attributes include strength (str), dexterity (dex), constitution (con), intelligence (int), wisdom (wis), and charisma (cha).

## Step 2: Plan the query
We will use two variables: ?dhampir and ?gorgon, which will represent the mean attribute values for Dhampir and Gorgon, respectively. We will calculate the mean by summing up the attribute values and dividing by the count of beasts for each type.

The query will involve joining the Beast class with the relevant attributes and filtering by the beast category names "Dhampir" and "Gorgon". We will use the SUM and COUNT functions to calculate the mean.

